                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7fc8da75-12f1-3a9c-a326-afda9bd04192",
                        "entry_id": "d5523214-71bb-3677-b63c-6b05b4e7105d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Gruppe von niederfränkischen Dialekten, die in der niederländischen Provinz Zeeland und auf der nördlich von Seeland gelegenen ehemaligen Insel Goeree-Overflakkee gesprochen werden."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c853771b-7eb5-4833-b516-72df05e3e1c5",
                        "source_entry_id": "d5523214-71bb-3677-b63c-6b05b4e7105d",
                        "source_sense_id": "7fc8da75-12f1-3a9c-a326-afda9bd04192",
                        "target_lang_word": "Zealandic",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Zealandic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "17b33bc6-8994-363c-b38e-6a0a2143ab24",
                                        "entry_id": "8c049228-247f-33bb-9458-abddb041e635",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The dialect of Danish spoken in Zealand, island in the North Sea."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "25e02d23-8d50-41b8-bf11-ee959e24aa61",
                                                "sense_id": "17b33bc6-8994-363c-b38e-6a0a2143ab24",
                                                "text": "This \"Danish\" in fact reflected local dialects; a standard language did not yet exist. But a certain dominance of Zealandic forms is visible already in the late Middle Ages: the administrative, ecclesiastical and commercial center of Denmark lay on Zealand (Roskilde, Copenhagen), and a Zealandic chancery style (inspired by German and Latin syntax) was developing."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4875260b-aa5e-40fb-b87b-f5af631bce8a",
                                                "sense_id": "17b33bc6-8994-363c-b38e-6a0a2143ab24",
                                                "text": "Here it seems natural to pay attention to some North-east Zealandic names ending in -rum, viz. Wigarum, AEsarum (and Niartherum ?)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "855e4178-55ed-48d9-8abd-cd5c16426d56",
                                                "sense_id": "17b33bc6-8994-363c-b38e-6a0a2143ab24",
                                                "text": "...the extent of the deflectional changes varies among the dialects, Jutish always having gone the furthest, Scanian always the most conservative, with Zealandic taking an intermediate position."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c0172a65-df13-3794-a922-67c05d396c6a",
                                        "entry_id": "8c049228-247f-33bb-9458-abddb041e635",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative spelling of Zeelandic, a language spoken in Zeeland, province of the Netherlands."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e9289e9c-53ee-43d2-94e1-dceee99db3cc",
                                                "sense_id": "c0172a65-df13-3794-a922-67c05d396c6a",
                                                "text": "In Zealandic Dutch ben- is the stem for the present tense for all persons except for 3SG (is)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "998e100d-fd93-4490-a64e-6ebd58baf91b",
                                                "sense_id": "c0172a65-df13-3794-a922-67c05d396c6a",
                                                "text": "Within Middle Dutch we can distinguish five large dialect groups: Flemish (including Zealandic), sometimes subdivided into West and East Flemish, was spoken in the modern region ofWest and East Flanders (Ghent, Bruges, Courtray); Brabantian was the language of the area covered by the modern Dutch province of North Brabant and the Belgian provinces of Brabant and Antwerp; Hollandic was mainly used in the present day provinces of North and South Holland and parts of Utrecht, while the people in Limburg (now a part of the Netherlands and Belgium) communicated in the Limburgish dialect."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6b6158ba-233e-466c-8a1c-f248c41d7df1",
                                                "sense_id": "c0172a65-df13-3794-a922-67c05d396c6a",
                                                "text": "Zealandic has a southern lexicon and there is no trace of a partially southern lexicon in Afrikaans."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Zealandic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b859ed0e-da33-3e55-ad97-48b0eb2f5f71",
                                        "entry_id": "bda84d69-b313-3ed2-ac9e-3e14439d6ad0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Pertaining to the Danish island of Zealand."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bbea7771-472c-4318-bf2e-20e22b3cc7ba",
                                                "sense_id": "b859ed0e-da33-3e55-ad97-48b0eb2f5f71",
                                                "text": "At the same time he was able — outside the Church— to captivate entirely different audiences by discovering and exploiting the kind of language they understood and the subjects that appealed to them: students, artisans and, at political meetings, sometimes sailors and sometimes Zealandic farmers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "30d6dd00-831a-43aa-8364-4e63c52a7d2e",
                                                "sense_id": "b859ed0e-da33-3e55-ad97-48b0eb2f5f71",
                                                "text": "But why had some Zealandic peasants suddenly become so involved in church discipline and more Gregorian than many Danish clerics of the time?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ac237247-47b7-41ab-9320-ee98938951d4",
                                                "sense_id": "b859ed0e-da33-3e55-ad97-48b0eb2f5f71",
                                                "text": "Districts are mentioned in a royal charter from 1085 by which King Knud IV (r.1080–1086; later canonized) donated land in a number of Scanian and Zealandic districts to the cathedral chapter of Lund."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5fd84508-e247-34ea-804b-f13dea85e295",
                                        "entry_id": "bda84d69-b313-3ed2-ac9e-3e14439d6ad0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Pertaining to the central standard Danish dialect."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2a74efd7-1d0c-4849-9732-651459a90bf2",
                        "source_entry_id": "d5523214-71bb-3677-b63c-6b05b4e7105d",
                        "source_sense_id": "7fc8da75-12f1-3a9c-a326-afda9bd04192",
                        "target_lang_word": "zélandais",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "zélandais",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4989c0ca-1a66-36d0-93c0-805c6a158c8d",
                                        "entry_id": "a840aa7b-bd44-3fc5-bb55-ff2d19887154",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Relatif à la Zélande, à ses habitants, les Zélandais."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6b3902cd-bbf1-43ee-9c05-aaba820e185a",
                                                "sense_id": "4989c0ca-1a66-36d0-93c0-805c6a158c8d",
                                                "text": "Elle avait le visage encadré, caché presque au fond d’une grande coiffe zélandaise qu’Abel lui avait rapportée de voyage et qu’elle avait mise aussitôt."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64e6683b-7fe8-427e-8d56-3e4bf007a305",
                                                "sense_id": "4989c0ca-1a66-36d0-93c0-805c6a158c8d",
                                                "text": "A voir la demeure, on l'eût dit échappée de quelque petite ville zélandaise, tant elle était menue et proprette."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "91b33d7b-7a5b-42fb-8e03-d6085a6d7017",
                                                "sense_id": "4989c0ca-1a66-36d0-93c0-805c6a158c8d",
                                                "text": "Actuellement, le consommateur n’a en effet aucune certitude sur le fait qu’une moule zélandaise provienne bien des eaux de Zélande."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "zélandais",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "85f49a8d-1028-3591-a051-dab8d5f18127",
                                        "entry_id": "1d663b56-918d-3c15-9514-2d0ba035254b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Langue régionale parlée aux Pays-Bas, dans la province de Zélande et dans l’île de Goeree-Overflakkee."
                                        ],
